# Server TypeScript

- Session mutations go through `SessionStore.apply` / `applyEvent` — do not fork write logic in HTTP vs MCP.
- MCP (`server/mcp.ts`) should keep calling the HTTP API so WebSocket clients stay in sync.
- Persist under `sessions/`; do not commit session JSON.
- Public functions: JSDoc. Prefer explicit types from `server/session/types.ts`.
- After protocol changes, update `AGENTS.md` and MCP tool descriptions together.
